                                           ;*	Microchip Technology Inc. 2002					*                                          C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*	Assembler version: 2.0000					*                                               C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*	Filename: 							*                                                            C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*		p18demo.asm (main routine)   				*                                           C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*	Dependents:							*                                                           C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*		p18lcd.asm						*                                                            C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*		p18math.asm						*                                                           C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*		16f877.lkr						*                                                            C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*	March 14,2002							*                                                         C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;* 	PICDEM 2 PLUS DEMO code. The following functions are included 	*             C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*	with this code:							*                                                       C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*		1. Voltmeter						*                                                          C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*			The center tap of R16 is connected to RA0, the	*                            C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*			A/D converter converts this analog voltage and	*                            C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*			the result is displayed on the LCD in a range	*                             C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*			from 0.00V - 5.00V.				*                                                    C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*		2. Buzzer						*                                                             C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*			The Piezo buzzer is connected to RC2 and is	*                               C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*			driven by the CCP1 module. The period and duty	*                            C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*			cycle are adjustable on the fly through the LCD	*                           C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*			and push-buttons.				*                                                      C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*		3. Temperature						*                                                        C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*			A TC74 Serial Digital Thermal Sensor is used to	*                           C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*			measure ambient temperature. The PIC and TC74	*                             C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;* 			communicate using the MSSP module. The TC74 is	*                           C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*			connected to the SDA & SCL I/O pins of the PIC	*                            C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*			and functions as a slave. Every 2 seconds, the	*                            C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*			temperature is logged into the external EEPROM  *                           C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*			in a specific memory location.			*                                          C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*		4. Clock						*                                                              C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*			This function is a real-time clock. When the	*                              C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*			mode is entered, time begins at 00:00:00. The 	*                            C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*			user can set the time if desired.		*                                        C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*									*                                                                     C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*		The data that is sent to the LCD is also sent to the	*                       C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*		USART through the RS-232 port to be displayed on a PC	*                      C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;*		HyperTerminal.						*                                                        C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
                                           ;************************************************************************        C:\d\Projects\LCDS\oc19\18\P18pt.ASM
